==English==

===Etymology===
From French [[socle#French|socle]], from Italian [[zoccolo]] ‘wooden shoe’, from Latin [[socculus]], diminutive of [[soccus]] ‘sock’.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsəʊkəl/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|əʊkəl|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
{{wikipedia}}

# {{context|architecture|lang=en}} A low [[plinth]] or [[pedestal]] used to display a statue or other art work.
# {{context|mathematics|lang=en}} The sum of the minimal [[submodule]]s of a given R-[[module]] of a given [[ring]] R.
# {{context|mathematics|group theory|lang=en}} The [[subgroup]] generated by the minimal [[normal subgroup]]s of a given [[group]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|a plinth or pedestal}} [[zocco]], [[zocle]]

====Translations====
{{trans-top|a plinth or pedestal}}
